claimed: free-row-variance — the last cheap lever named at the end of merge-scaling-shape: Writer.widen rebuilds EVERY Free node per element (twice per merge, once per source) purely because "Free stays invariant in its row". But Writer[+W,+A] is already covariant, and F appears in Free only in covariant positions (Inject's field, Bind's Free-typed field and its continuation's RESULT). If `enum Free[+F[+_], A]` typechecks, then Free[Writer % A + G, X] <: Free[Writer % (A|B) + G, X] by subtyping and widen becomes free -- removing a whole per-element tree-rebuild pass from every merge. Try it, measure it, land or decline on data.
